{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2d23536aa1a1853b","name":"Beck-tori","source":{"id":"source:reference-2d23536aa1a1853b","title":"Beck-tori","revision":16184,"timestamp":"2024-08-18T00:56:27Z","sha256":"cc5f2b5651dd17aba22c813bcf6f1ae001b55c7c4093bd9819ccc42f86a630eb","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=16184","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Beck-tori&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2d23536aa1a1853b","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Beck-tori are aquatic, Force-sensitive parasites that grow to extreme size. A Beck-tori resembles a flat, elongated leech, with a raspy underside covered in spines used to flay flesh. The Beck-tori uses the corpse of its prey as a host for its eggs. When they hatch, Beck-tori larvae pose little threat. Left undisturbed, however, Beck-tori can live for centuries and grow that entire time. Colossal Beck-tori have been spotted on water-rich planets such as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Naboo"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Naboo","referenceId":"reference:8c2767dbc8d173d5"}," and are grave threats to any seafaring community. An accidental infestation on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dac"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dac","referenceId":"reference:8654fc7bdc8fd9cb"}," decimated entire ecosystems and took nearly 50 years to repair. They are brutish, aggressive creatures that blindly attack anything that moves. Reports indicate that Beck-tori even assault boats or repulsorlift craft that skim too closely to the surface.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Beck-tori use their Force abilities to sense prey and bolster their fighting prowess. They are subconsciously drawn to other Force-sensitive creatures, making them dangerous opponents against Jedi.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Beck-tori Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Beck-tori are usually found in aquatic environments, where their ability to use ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," throws an added twist to the hazards in or near water. The Beck-tori shown here represents a healthy adult, which is usually more than a match for any opponent. Juveniles are typically Medium size, and ancient Beck-tori are Gargantuan or larger.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Beck-tori Statistics (CL 12)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge Aquatic ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 13\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Low-Light Vision"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Low-Light_Vision"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +5\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 30 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 30), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 28, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 22\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https